  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-79e18161-ce08-44f3-bc75-38464cf02996-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Exquisite Corpse is a collaborative drawing or writing game in which participants add to a work without seeing all of the earlier contributions. A folded sheet can conceal each section while leaving a few connecting marks or words visible. Unfolding it reveals a composition that no single participant planned."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-79e18161-ce08-44f3-bc75-38464cf02996-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Associated with Surrealist circles in 1920s Paris, the game turns restricted information and chance into tools for collective invention. It has no fixed winning condition: the unexpected whole, and the group’s response to it, are the point of the activity."
    },
    {
      "id": "31cde599-32e4-461f-8277-6197d328495c",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "0891379d-cc8a-4c96-a2b4-82c72eaf46d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "a01069de-90a7-4ce3-9676-81b6c23e1ff6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "A game in which each participant takes turns writing or drawing on a sheet of paper, folding it to conceal his or her contribution, and then passing it to the next player for a further contribution. The game gained popularity in artistic circles during the 1920s when it was adopted as a technique by artists of the Surrealist movement to generate collaborative compositions."
    },
    {
      "id": "8cb2e44d-2011-475a-bdbc-ba9b3ad50e61",
      "type": "paragraph",
